nodecode-buildpilot is a rewrite of Justnevo's Justnevo/buildpilot:

  https://github.com/Justnevo/buildpilot
  commit 037d8eda0ba53d741e4f0bcfdc246cc6bab1dcc7
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 BuildPilot contributors (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's whole surface, as Common Lisp against the Nodecode
cell contract. The six tools keep their names and their arguments
(add_project, list_projects, add_task, update_task, checkpoint,
get_project_context), the three task states are the same, and a project's
context is still its details, its tasks and its newest checkpoint in one
answer. The schema that was built in Python with CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS is
one JSON document holding the same three lists and the same id counters,
written atomically and created on first use; the SQLite driver and the
Python runtime are gone. list_projects gained an optional search over a
project's name and description, /buildpilot was added to show the store to a
person, and checkpoints_kept bounds how many checkpoints one project keeps.

Left out: the Python SQLite layer itself (sqlite3, its connection context
manager and the row-to-dict conversion), which the JSON document replaces,
and the Hermes profile directory the database path was derived from, which is
the Nodecode home here. Nothing of the original's behaviour was dropped: the
same six verbs, the same three tables' fields, and the same refusals on an
empty name, an unknown project, an unknown task and a status outside the
three.
